('111.6.b.8.C',4,'A movie starts at 2:00 and ends at 4:10. How many minutes long is the movie?','["110 minutes", "170 minutes", "130 minutes", "120 minutes"]'::jsonb,2,'From 2:00 to 4:10 is 130 minutes.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'A movie starts at 6:30 and ends at 8:15. How many minutes long is the movie?','["145 minutes", "95 minutes", "115 minutes", "105 minutes"]'::jsonb,3,'From 6:30 to 8:15 is 105 minutes.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'Sam buys 4 notebooks that cost $1.50 each and pays with a $10 bill. How much change should Sam get?','["$4.00", "$8.50", "$3.50", "$6.00"]'::jsonb,0,'4 × $1.50 = $6.00. $10.00 − $6.00 = $4.00.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'Cara buys 4 notebooks that cost $2.75 each and pays with a $20 bill. How much change should Cara get?','["$11.00", "$9.00", "$8.50", "$17.25"]'::jsonb,1,'4 × $2.75 = $11.00. $20.00 − $11.00 = $9.00.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'A pitcher holds 3 liters of juice. Ben pours out 450 milliliters. How many milliliters of juice are left?','["2,050 mL", "3,450 mL", "2,550 mL", "2,650 mL"]'::jsonb,2,'3 L = 3,000 mL. 3,000 − 450 = 2,550.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'A pitcher holds 2 liters of juice. Sam pours out 750 milliliters. How many milliliters of juice are left?','["1,350 mL", "750 mL", "2,750 mL", "1,250 mL"]'::jsonb,3,'2 L = 2,000 mL. 2,000 − 750 = 1,250.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'A bag of rice has a mass of 2 kilograms. Cara uses 1,200 grams. How many grams of rice are left?','["800 g", "900 g", "700 g", "1,300 g"]'::jsonb,0,'2 kg = 2,000 g. 2,000 − 1,200 = 800.','original'),
('111.6.b.8.C',4,'A bag of rice has a mass of 3 kilograms. Ben uses 450 grams. How many grams of rice are left?','["2,450 g", "2,550 g", "2,650 g", "3,450 g"]'::jsonb,1,'3 kg = 3,000 g. 3,000 − 450 = 2,550.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.A',2,'These scores were collected: 15, 18, 15, 18, 14, 14, 12, 18, 12, 10, 14, 12. If the data are put in a frequency table, what is the frequency of 18?','["12", "2", "3", "5"]'::jsonb,2,'Count how many times 18 appears: 3.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.A',2,'These scores were collected: 15, 15, 18, 10, 15, 10, 14, 14, 14, 18, 14, 15. If the data are put in a frequency table, what is the frequency of 18?','["3", "4", "1", "2"]'::jsonb,3,'Count how many times 18 appears: 2.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.A',2,'In a stem-and-leaf plot, one row is  6 | 0 1 2 5 8.  Which data values does this row show?','["60, 61, 62, 65, 68", "6, 7, 8, 11, 14", "6, 16, 26, 56, 86", "0, 1, 2, 5, 8"]'::jsonb,0,'The stem 6 is the tens digit and each leaf is a ones digit: 60, 61, 62, 65, 68.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.A',2,'In a stem-and-leaf plot, one row is  5 | 2 5 6.  Which data values does this row show?','["2, 5, 6", "52, 55, 56", "25, 55, 65", "7, 10, 11"]'::jsonb,1,'The stem 5 is the tens digit and each leaf is a ones digit: 52, 55, 56.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.A',3,'Which stem-and-leaf row shows the data values 80, 85, 86, 89?','["8 | 9 6 5 0 1", "8 | 80 85 86 89", "8 | 0 5 6 9", "0 | 8 5 6 9"]'::jsonb,2,'The stem 8 stands for the tens digit and the leaves are the ones digits.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.A',3,'Which stem-and-leaf row shows the data values 71, 72, 73?','["7 | 71 72 73", "1 | 7 2 3", "7 | 3 2 1 0", "7 | 1 2 3"]'::jsonb,3,'The stem 7 stands for the tens digit and the leaves are the ones digits.','original'),
('111.6.b.9.B',4,'A stem-and-leaf plot shows the number of books students read:  1 | 3 4 6  2 | 3 5 7 9  3 | 0 7  4 | 0 7.  How many students read more than 25 books?','["6", "11", "5", "7"]'::jsonb,0,'Count the values greater than 25: 6.','original'),
