('111.6.b.3.F',3,'Maya says 3/8 + 2/8 = 5/16. Which explains her mistake?','["She should have subtracted.", "She should have multiplied the numerators.", "She should have added the denominators.", "When the denominators are the same, the denominator stays the same: the answer is 5/8."]'::jsonb,3,'Add only the numerators when the denominators match.','original'),
('111.6.b.3.F',3,'Eli adds 1/2 + 3/4. About how large is the sum?','["greater than 1", "less than 1", "less than 1/2", "exactly 1/2"]'::jsonb,0,'1/2 + 3/4 is more than 1/2 + 1/2 = 1, so the sum is greater than 1.','original'),
('111.6.b.3.C',2,'Which statement about equivalent fractions is true?','["They always have the same numerator.", "They name the same amount of the same whole.", "They name different amounts.", "They always have the same denominator."]'::jsonb,1,'Equivalent fractions name the same point on the number line.','original'),
('111.6.b.3.D',3,'Which comparison is true?','["1/2 < 3/8", "1/2 = 3/8", "1/2 > 3/8", "3/8 > 5/8"]'::jsonb,2,'1/2 = 4/8, and 4/8 is greater than 3/8.','original'),
('111.6.b.3.D',3,'Which fraction is the greatest?','["1/4", "3/8", "1/2", "3/4"]'::jsonb,3,'3/4 is greater than 1/2, and 1/2 is greater than 3/8 and 1/4.','original'),
('111.6.b.3.D',3,'A friend says 1/8 is greater than 1/4 because 8 is greater than 4. What is wrong?','["More equal parts means smaller parts, so 1/8 is less than 1/4.", "8 is not greater than 4.", "1/8 and 1/4 are equal.", "Nothing is wrong."]'::jsonb,0,'A bigger denominator (with the same numerator) means smaller pieces.','original'),
('111.6.b.3.E',3,'Which equation is true?','["5/8 + 2/8 = 10/8", "5/8 + 2/8 = 7/8", "5/8 + 2/8 = 3/8", "5/8 + 2/8 = 7/16"]'::jsonb,1,'Add the numerators and keep the denominator: 5 + 2 = 7.','original'),
('111.6.b.4.E',3,'A 3-row array has 24 counters in all. Which equation matches finding the number of counters in each row?','["24 + 3 = □", "24 × 3 = □", "24 ÷ 3 = □", "3 − 24 = □"]'::jsonb,2,'Splitting 24 into 3 equal rows is 24 ÷ 3.','original'),
('111.6.b.4.F',3,'Maya divides 612 by 3 and gets 24. Which tells whether the answer is reasonable?','["Yes, because 6 ÷ 3 = 2", "No, because 612 is odd", "Yes, because 24 is less than 612", "No, because 3 × 24 = 72, which is not 612"]'::jsonb,3,'Check with multiplication: 3 × 24 = 72, not 612. The correct answer is 204.','original'),
('111.6.b.4.H',3,'A remainder of 3 when dividing by 8 means:','["3 items are left over after making equal groups of 8", "the answer is 3 more than 8", "3 groups of 8 were made", "the groups are not equal"]'::jsonb,0,'A remainder is what is left after making as many equal groups as possible.','original'),
('111.6.b.5.C',2,'Which formula can be used to find the perimeter of a rectangle with length l and width w?','["P = l × w", "P = 2l + 2w", "P = 4l", "P = l + w"]'::jsonb,1,'A rectangle has 2 lengths and 2 widths: 2l + 2w.','original'),
('111.6.b.5.C',2,'Which formula can be used to find the area of a rectangle with length l and width w?','["A = l + w", "A = 2l + 2w", "A = l × w", "A = 4s"]'::jsonb,2,'Area counts the unit squares: length × width.','original'),
('111.6.b.5.C',2,'Which formula can be used to find the perimeter of a square with side length s?','["P = s + 4", "P = s × s", "P = 2s", "P = 4s"]'::jsonb,3,'A square has 4 equal sides.','original'),
('111.6.b.5.C',3,'Which two measurements have the same units?','["perimeter in feet and a side length in feet", "area in square feet and a side in feet", "area in feet and perimeter in square feet", "area in square feet and perimeter in feet"]'::jsonb,0,'Perimeter is a length, so it is measured in feet, like a side. Area uses square units.','original'),
